Ladybird fits and positions canvas content using the same replaced-
element geometry as images and video. Canvas surfaces and bitmap output
use the canvas attribute dimensions, scaled for CSS zoom. Overflow is
clipped to the canvas content box.

Blink’s HTMLCanvasPainter::PaintReplaced uses ReplacedContentRect, with
LayoutHTMLCanvas::CanvasSizeChanged providing zoomed canvas dimensions.
WebKit’s RenderHTMLCanvas::paintReplaced uses replacedContentRect and
clips the result to the content box; canvasSizeChanged supplies zoomed
attribute dimensions. Gecko’s nsHTMLCanvasFrame::GetDestRect uses the
canvas dimensions with nsLayoutUtils::ComputeObjectDestRect, applying
the object-fit and object-position properties through that shared path.

Bitmap-renderer output retains the canvas attribute dimensions even
when the bitmap has a different aspect ratio. Chrome confirms this
behavior. It preserves the intentional deviation from HTML’s natural-
size rule for the output bitmap, without changing layout on transfer.
For a zero-width canvas with valid bitmap output, Chrome fills the
content box. This matches the empty-size fallback in Blink’s
ComputeObjectFitAndPositionRect and WebKit’s replacedContentRect.

The imported canvas WPTs match their references in Chrome. Other
controls cover bitmap-renderer output with mismatched dimensions, an
OffscreenCanvas placeholder, cover clipping, CSS zoom with edge offsets,
a zero-width canvas containing a transferred bitmap, and natural sizes
that round to zero under small CSS zoom.
